WEBVTT

00:00.720 --> 00:02.740
Don't hurt me...

00:04.040 --> 00:05.960
Spare me...

00:06.740 --> 00:11.990
Don't hurt me... Spare me...

00:07.700 --> 00:10.860
I have the same dream a lot.

00:13.200 --> 00:15.620
You had your fun for a while, didn't you?

00:15.620 --> 00:18.990
You paid a high price for it, though, Doc.

00:19.740 --> 00:24.070
Don't hurt me... Spare me...

00:24.610 --> 00:26.280
You're disgusting!

00:28.430 --> 00:32.730
Don't hurt me... Spare me...

00:33.120 --> 00:36.780
Don't hurt me... Spare...

00:39.340 --> 00:44.920
And for a while after I wake up,
I just lie there afraid,

00:44.920 --> 00:49.030
unsure if I'm awake
or still in the nightmare.

00:50.410 --> 00:53.590
Don't hurt me...

00:54.030 --> 01:05.870
Ningen Fushin: Adventurers Who Don't
Believe in Humanity Will Save the World

02:24.540 --> 02:29.460
"Labyrinth Dragnet"

02:26.050 --> 02:27.010
Wha—

02:30.260 --> 02:31.830
You're paying for that.

02:34.130 --> 02:36.380
I still can't believe we were right.

02:36.380 --> 02:39.280
I've never seen anybody
who can move like that.

02:39.280 --> 02:43.520
She was just like the Stepping Man we saw.

02:43.520 --> 02:47.380
I refuse to accept that
was Stepping Man, though!

02:47.380 --> 02:50.620
She was writing articles
about herself? Nonsense!

02:51.030 --> 02:52.860
Sorry to interrupt.

02:53.840 --> 02:58.190
I've got a pretty girl who wants to see you.
Not as pretty as me, of course.

02:58.830 --> 03:00.900
That's something to look forward to.

03:03.900 --> 03:05.010
Mom!

03:05.580 --> 03:08.170
You're the Survivors, right?

03:08.690 --> 03:11.300
You're all healed up now, Ada?

03:11.630 --> 03:15.110
I guess I'm famous and I didn't know it.

03:15.110 --> 03:17.670
What, you know her?

03:17.670 --> 03:21.540
The swashbuckler of the legendary
A-Rank party Grandchef.

03:21.540 --> 03:25.560
"Ada the Sommelier".
She's been famous for ages.

03:26.520 --> 03:29.020
There's a name I haven't heard in a while.

03:29.020 --> 03:32.560
Yeah, I went on the Adventure of the
Platinum Peach with Fifs and his gang.

03:32.560 --> 03:36.070
Fifs? Fifs the Solo Eater?

03:36.070 --> 03:38.800
I've heard he's S-Rank right now.

03:38.800 --> 03:41.310
But back then, we were all young.

03:43.700 --> 03:47.020
First, sorry for the trouble
my daughter caused you.

03:47.020 --> 03:48.450
I'm sorry!

03:48.900 --> 03:51.830
She's too fearless for her own good.
I don't know who she gets it from.

03:53.100 --> 03:57.010
But she's done with Stepping Man.

03:57.010 --> 03:58.540
That's right.

03:58.540 --> 04:00.720
Don't do anything dangerous anymore.

04:00.990 --> 04:02.080
But, Master...

04:02.770 --> 04:05.440
Master? What's that about?

04:05.440 --> 04:08.400
Mom, I want him to make me his student!

04:08.400 --> 04:10.290
Listen, kid...

04:10.290 --> 04:14.110
Reina, I want to make this clear right now.

04:14.910 --> 04:17.350
To me, you're an enemy.

04:19.710 --> 04:23.200
Maybe "enemy" is going too far.

04:23.200 --> 04:30.400
But whenever I see a girl
your age, I get so scared.

04:32.280 --> 04:36.930
A long time ago, a certain girl deceived me.

04:37.820 --> 04:42.640
And because of that, I spent years in jail.

04:42.640 --> 04:46.700
When I got out, just the
sight of a girl was enough

04:46.700 --> 04:53.210
to make me freeze in terror, to the
point where I could barely speak...

04:53.740 --> 04:56.270
If it was just words,
that would be one thing,

04:56.900 --> 04:59.750
but, at times, I can barely breathe.

05:00.320 --> 05:05.720
That goes for any girl
your age. Not just you.

05:05.720 --> 05:08.910
But you protected me!

05:09.720 --> 05:10.860
That's...

05:11.600 --> 05:16.660
That's just what anyone would have done
if they saw a young child in danger.

05:18.900 --> 05:19.990
But...

05:21.920 --> 05:24.170
It surprised me.

05:25.050 --> 05:30.800
It made me feel something akin to hope...

05:31.180 --> 05:37.140
Hope that maybe I could move on,
maybe I could get over this...

05:39.420 --> 05:41.490
And that's why you said in fifteen years?

05:41.490 --> 05:43.400
What are you talking about?

05:43.400 --> 05:45.420
I won't let you marry her!

05:45.420 --> 05:47.420
She ain't marrying no adventurer!

05:47.420 --> 05:50.800
No, ma'am. It's nothing like that.

05:50.800 --> 05:51.940
That's right, Mom!

05:52.200 --> 05:55.570
He's my master, not my boyfriend!

05:55.570 --> 05:58.940
If I was picking a boyfriend,
I'd be more careful!

05:58.940 --> 05:59.840
Oh, my.

06:00.280 --> 06:01.710
She's smart for her age.

06:04.330 --> 06:06.710
I think you just got rejected, Zem.

06:07.260 --> 06:10.840
Fifteen years from now,
she'd totally be my type...

06:12.120 --> 06:14.540
As a former member of Grandchef...

06:15.030 --> 06:18.040
Do you want me to slice you
into finely fileted strips?

06:17.260 --> 06:19.840
Please, no!

06:24.200 --> 06:26.750
Okay, I think I see what's going on, now.

06:26.750 --> 06:28.800
You really were there when
she needed help, huh?

06:29.340 --> 06:31.140
Let me thank you again.

06:31.630 --> 06:35.620
But you need to give this up, too, Survivors.

06:37.120 --> 06:39.630
Just forget this whole thing.

06:39.950 --> 06:42.450
You understand, if you fought it, right?

06:42.450 --> 06:45.080
We can't defeat it.

06:46.180 --> 06:49.130
We don't have to take orders
from you there, Ms. Grandchef.

06:49.680 --> 06:52.730
If an adventurer wants to go
after a bounty, he's free to.

06:54.160 --> 06:56.550
You're not strong enough right now.

06:56.550 --> 06:57.890
Of that I'm aware,

06:58.190 --> 07:02.370
but I can't sit idly by and
allow these kidnappings to happen.

07:02.370 --> 07:05.960
That's the Solar Knights' job.

07:05.960 --> 07:06.660
Yup.

07:07.250 --> 07:13.670
But I don't like the way she's using an
urban legend as cover to kidnap kids.

07:14.240 --> 07:17.680
And I took advantage of that.

07:18.540 --> 07:24.560
The Solar Knights are too busy to respond
to every single kidnapping case.

07:27.580 --> 07:32.100
So you decided to pretend the
kidnapper was the Stepping Man,

07:32.100 --> 07:35.430
use the bounty, and get the
adventurers to go after him.

07:40.300 --> 07:42.390
I'm out of this business, though.

07:42.390 --> 07:48.080
I don't want her to do something dumb
and get caught up something bad,

07:48.080 --> 07:51.120
and I don't want to die and
leave her without a mom.

07:51.120 --> 07:52.940
That's the right move.

07:53.270 --> 07:55.560
You said we're not strong enough
to win right now, right?

07:56.210 --> 07:59.720
Then tell us how we can win.

08:02.130 --> 08:06.220
Your leader bows his head and
begs for help that easily?

08:07.850 --> 08:08.700
Yes, actually.

08:09.090 --> 08:11.210
He decided it was the logical thing to do.

08:11.210 --> 08:13.370
That's what makes Nick great!

08:13.720 --> 08:15.720
Sea Anemone

08:13.720 --> 08:15.720
Southgate Legal
is 2F♥

08:14.130 --> 08:16.640
Drink this first.

08:18.270 --> 08:19.230
What is it?

08:19.230 --> 08:22.470
This smell... this is glory mushroom soup?

08:22.470 --> 08:26.050
Your sense of smell's amazing, Curran!

08:26.050 --> 08:28.740
It's an expensive soup that never
goes for less than 50,000 dinah!

08:32.280 --> 08:33.660
It's good.

08:33.660 --> 08:37.620
So what's this soup got
to do with our victory?

08:37.950 --> 08:40.500
It's not a good luck charm
or anything, right?

08:40.500 --> 08:44.000
These mushrooms will draw out
your latent magical potential.

08:45.620 --> 08:47.960
Fighting Stepping Man means
a lot of jumping around

08:47.960 --> 08:52.620
and switching between melee
attacks and dodging.

08:52.620 --> 08:56.250
What'll determine your victory
is how you use your magic.

08:56.570 --> 08:58.480
Magic, huh?

08:58.480 --> 09:01.450
I don't think that's my thing...

09:01.450 --> 09:04.640
And I can't cast while in melee range...

09:04.640 --> 09:07.260
We casters spend our time
in the back, after all...

09:07.260 --> 09:11.980
I'd like to try it, but I'm
not good with complex stuff.

09:11.980 --> 09:15.790
Oh, my.
You Survivors sure are quick to give up.

09:15.790 --> 09:18.330
I don't need advice.

09:19.370 --> 09:21.900
Hold this in your hand and
say this word in your mind:

09:22.200 --> 09:24.190
"Burn".

09:24.190 --> 09:25.390
An Igniter?

09:27.010 --> 09:28.450
Curran, right?

09:28.450 --> 09:29.960
You first.

09:29.960 --> 09:31.180
O-Okay...

09:32.820 --> 09:35.450
Burn! Burn! Burn!

09:36.690 --> 09:38.090
Relax.

09:39.780 --> 09:42.160
Focus your mind on the area
around your belly button.

09:44.050 --> 09:45.310
It's not working!

09:45.570 --> 09:47.520
I can't do this!

09:47.520 --> 09:49.680
If I want fire, I can just breathe it!

09:50.150 --> 09:53.080
You're having trouble focusing, aren't you?

09:53.080 --> 09:55.150
Well, take your time.

09:55.730 --> 09:56.560
Next.

09:56.890 --> 10:01.120
I've never been a mage...

10:05.580 --> 10:07.140
You did it, Nick!

10:07.140 --> 10:08.350
Wow!

10:09.510 --> 10:11.220
You're the best, Nick!

10:12.410 --> 10:14.690
I'm surprised I could do that, sure.

10:14.690 --> 10:18.090
But a flame that size won't even
drive away one of the city's thugs.

10:18.460 --> 10:21.000
I'm not telling you to fight with fire.

10:21.000 --> 10:23.090
I just wanted to see your potential.

10:23.090 --> 10:25.860
And? How'd I do?

10:27.850 --> 10:29.350
Well...

10:30.180 --> 10:31.800
Depends on how hard you train.

10:35.680 --> 10:40.740
Stepping Man uses two enhancement spells:
Light Body and Heavy Body.

10:41.150 --> 10:44.620
Those of you who'll be fighting directly,
start with Light Body.

10:44.910 --> 10:47.030
Give me ten jumps.

10:48.990 --> 10:50.760
If that's all...

10:51.800 --> 10:54.240
One, two...

10:54.830 --> 10:57.140
Three, four...

10:57.570 --> 11:00.000
Five... wow!

11:00.290 --> 11:01.130
Seven...

11:01.520 --> 11:03.650
Eight, nine—

11:08.350 --> 11:11.510
N-Nine...

11:13.050 --> 11:16.230
I thought you had the most potential, but...

11:30.830 --> 11:32.440
If we know the hours you're out hunting,

11:32.440 --> 11:34.290
and where you hunt, you're as good as ours.

11:34.690 --> 11:37.400
Why always the same time, though?

11:37.400 --> 11:39.990
Are you Olivia?

11:45.080 --> 11:45.810
Wait!

11:49.110 --> 11:52.590
Isn't he Olivia?

11:52.590 --> 11:56.300
Attack magic, movement magic,
and illusion magic at the same time.

11:56.680 --> 12:00.430
Could any mage really do all that at once?

12:00.430 --> 12:03.500
So one of them must be a magic item?

12:03.500 --> 12:04.830
Yeah...

12:05.140 --> 12:10.710
I know what's on the store shelves, but I
don't know anything about rare artifacts.

12:11.310 --> 12:13.820
We know someone who does, though.

12:20.230 --> 12:22.740
So? You didn't come all this
way just to recommend me

12:22.740 --> 12:25.710
the dragonian's favorite meat buns, right?

12:26.380 --> 12:28.220
I want your help.

12:29.730 --> 12:33.610
Do you know of any magic items that can
hide your presence or disguise you?

12:34.720 --> 12:35.970
That'd be...

12:39.340 --> 12:41.150
the Illusion King's Jewel.

12:42.000 --> 12:45.220
Or more specifically, a magic
item that incorporates it.

12:45.220 --> 12:47.180
That's awfully specific.

12:49.010 --> 12:50.280
How do I deal with it?

12:50.280 --> 12:53.010
Breaking the illusion isn't that hard.

12:53.010 --> 12:59.110
The easiest way to shut it down for
sure is to speak the user's name.

13:00.720 --> 13:03.390
Are you Olivia?

13:04.390 --> 13:07.510
You can't just say names randomly, though.

13:07.960 --> 13:12.070
You're strengthening the idea in your
mind that it has to be that person.

13:12.070 --> 13:14.890
So if your mind's not
certain, it won't work.

13:15.120 --> 13:16.890
It's gotta be the first name you say.

13:18.310 --> 13:21.740
It's not Olivia... then?

13:35.550 --> 13:37.550
Come on! One more time!

13:37.550 --> 13:39.350
No time to rest!

13:39.350 --> 13:40.560
O-Okay!

13:41.200 --> 13:43.860
It's been forever since I've
had to train this hard.

13:44.310 --> 13:47.310
It reminds me of the old days...

13:53.780 --> 13:58.920
He who truly becomes a master of war can
destroy a monster without any weapons.

13:59.440 --> 14:02.530
First, focus on nothing but
learning to improve yourself!

14:13.120 --> 14:16.070
You can learn magic after that.

14:16.420 --> 14:17.950
Y-Yes, sir!

14:18.560 --> 14:23.260
You won't get that much taller.
Your parents were short.

14:23.260 --> 14:24.090
Yes, sir!

14:24.480 --> 14:26.470
But being short isn't a weakness!

14:26.470 --> 14:29.590
Find what you're good at and increase the
number of things that make you strong!

14:32.360 --> 14:33.340
Yes, sir!

14:46.480 --> 14:48.600
Are you about ready?

14:49.430 --> 14:52.580
No. The magic spell ends
if I'm not focusing.

14:52.890 --> 14:55.870
It'd be hard to do a fight like this.

14:57.180 --> 15:00.260
I used the files Ada had to
go around and ask questions

15:00.260 --> 15:02.970
about leaky roofs and people
getting their roofs fixed.

15:02.970 --> 15:04.480
I see!

15:04.480 --> 15:06.870
He jumps from roof to roof.

15:06.870 --> 15:09.800
If we look at where the damage
is concentrated, then...

15:09.800 --> 15:10.830
Yup.

15:10.830 --> 15:12.480
We can narrow it down.

15:14.050 --> 15:15.380
This is...

15:19.460 --> 15:21.230
Any new info?

15:21.230 --> 15:24.740
Two of Greg's puppies died.

15:24.740 --> 15:27.600
His 20 percent discount is over,
'cause he figures it's bad luck.

15:28.770 --> 15:32.230
And somebody brought a child's
body to the common graves.

15:32.540 --> 15:34.390
Nothing new.

15:34.870 --> 15:36.450
A child's body.

15:37.030 --> 15:40.080
A boy? Or a girl?

15:41.210 --> 15:42.870
I don't remember.

15:42.870 --> 15:47.950
I don't remember if they had
short hair or long hair, even.

15:48.770 --> 15:50.550
It happens all the time.

15:52.290 --> 15:54.850
I don't like this.

15:56.660 --> 15:57.780
Be careful.

15:58.800 --> 16:00.270
Telepathy?

16:00.270 --> 16:01.380
What is it?

16:01.650 --> 16:03.640
We're being followed.

16:04.500 --> 16:07.020
We could be attacked at any moment.

16:15.390 --> 16:17.280
I just learned that stuff.
Will it work on her?

16:17.280 --> 16:18.400
Light Body!

16:23.750 --> 16:26.910
Light Body. I knew you were Stepping Man.

16:27.180 --> 16:28.800
No, you're Stepping Man!

16:35.120 --> 16:36.060
Parallel!

16:37.420 --> 16:38.470
No way!

16:38.470 --> 16:39.420
Parallel!

16:40.190 --> 16:41.240
Seriously?

16:43.220 --> 16:45.820
I stopped your best move.

16:47.370 --> 16:50.520
Be certain... and speak their name.

16:51.360 --> 16:52.460
Olivia!

16:52.820 --> 16:54.310
You're Olivia, right?

17:00.510 --> 17:02.320
Yes, I am Olivia!

17:03.150 --> 17:05.340
Oh, if it isn't Nick?

17:05.340 --> 17:07.030
It's me, Olivia!

17:07.030 --> 17:09.330
The Olivia you suspected
of being Stepping Man!

17:09.330 --> 17:11.590
Not that I hold it against you
or hate you for it, though!

17:11.590 --> 17:13.590
But, some nights, I did cry myself to sleep!

17:13.590 --> 17:16.580
Yes, it is I, Olivia!

17:17.550 --> 17:19.850
Let's try and figure this out...

17:19.850 --> 17:20.850
So, basically...

17:21.260 --> 17:24.050
You're Stepping Man, right, Nick?

17:24.050 --> 17:25.350
Obviously, I'm not!

17:25.770 --> 17:28.940
We were pretty sure you were
actually Stepping Man...

17:30.260 --> 17:31.730
Well...

17:32.420 --> 17:34.360
Don't get too surprised.

17:34.360 --> 17:37.860
But not only am I a reporter,
and an adventurer,

17:38.160 --> 17:40.150
I am also Stepping Man!

17:40.150 --> 17:41.380
We know.

17:41.670 --> 17:45.360
Or actually, that's just
what they used to call me.

17:45.630 --> 17:47.120
What's going on?

17:47.120 --> 17:49.680
So you're Stepping Man, right?

17:53.480 --> 17:58.000
I'm not the Stepping Man everyone
knows for being a kidnapper, though!

17:58.340 --> 18:01.060
Basically, Stepping Man
is a name used to refer

18:01.060 --> 18:04.900
to every weirdo that jumps around
the city's roofs at night!

18:05.250 --> 18:07.830
So Olivia's true identity was "weirdo"?

18:07.830 --> 18:10.270
Well, we knew that a while ago.

18:10.270 --> 18:11.560
I see.

18:11.560 --> 18:15.050
I've never heard the
"Multiple Stepping Men" theory before.

18:15.050 --> 18:16.240
But...

18:16.240 --> 18:19.410
If you'd answered us instead of running,
we wouldn't have had to deal with this.

18:19.410 --> 18:20.880
Very true!

18:20.880 --> 18:25.280
I can't get anywhere near the guild or the
editing department anymore because of that.

18:26.880 --> 18:31.440
Oh, what was that thing you just did?
I heard you say "Parallel".

18:31.440 --> 18:32.310
My...

18:33.230 --> 18:38.250
"Mysterious Boy? Girl? Discovered Who Uses
Parallel, an Advanced Ancient Spell."

18:38.250 --> 18:41.080
Wouldn't that be a good article?

18:41.820 --> 18:45.360
Then maybe I'll just submit
an article to <i>Lemuria Monthly</i>

18:45.360 --> 18:48.790
about how Stepping Man is
actually a female reporter

18:48.790 --> 18:51.290
and a witch who uses ancient magic!

18:52.990 --> 18:58.560
Remember that we're under no obligation to
run every article that gets submitted...

18:59.680 --> 19:02.580
Well, let's just forget it for now.

19:02.580 --> 19:05.080
It feels like we're both
after the same thing.

19:05.080 --> 19:07.080
Y-Yes.

19:07.080 --> 19:11.730
Let's do our best to capture
Stepping Man together! Hip-hip hooray!

19:12.250 --> 19:14.080
Is that really okay?

19:30.220 --> 19:33.270
I don't see anything really unusual...

19:33.270 --> 19:34.510
Really?

19:36.620 --> 19:39.070
What does her face look like?

19:39.520 --> 19:42.830
Tell me specifics, as accurately as you can.

19:43.210 --> 19:46.320
What does her mouth look like?
Is it big? Small?

19:46.650 --> 19:48.590
Is her nose pronounced? Or flat?

19:48.590 --> 19:51.310
Her eyes? Any freckles? Or scars?

19:52.820 --> 19:55.340
I'm not sure what to say...

19:55.770 --> 19:58.270
She's got eyes, a nose...

19:59.910 --> 20:02.720
No, it's strange.

20:03.070 --> 20:05.400
It's strange how nothing's strange.

20:05.400 --> 20:06.570
Yes.

20:06.570 --> 20:07.860
It's strange.

20:07.860 --> 20:11.540
Everything about it is strange.

20:11.540 --> 20:15.750
Our recognition abilities are
being jammed on every level...

20:15.750 --> 20:17.490
Which means...

20:18.300 --> 20:20.740
Let's see what's beneath it.

20:31.220 --> 20:32.270
What's this?

20:32.660 --> 20:35.760
A fragment of the Illusion
King's Jewel, probably.

20:37.180 --> 20:41.260
Its jamming feature is small, but there.

20:41.260 --> 20:45.410
And that's how they got past the
Solar Knights' forensics team?

20:46.140 --> 20:48.130
But why?

20:59.020 --> 21:01.010
There's a burn mark on her arm...

21:01.010 --> 21:03.520
It looks old.

21:03.520 --> 21:05.540
There's a mole on her neck.

21:08.760 --> 21:11.030
Signs of treatment for
Yellow Demon Sickness.

21:11.390 --> 21:15.050
She's not a nameless corpse.

21:15.310 --> 21:19.690
She was precious to somebody.
Somebody loved her.

21:22.180 --> 21:25.300
Sea Anemone

21:22.180 --> 21:25.300
Southgate Legal
is 2F♥

21:26.120 --> 21:27.800
Martha Canning. Age 10.

21:28.150 --> 21:31.800
Daughter of a man who runs a shop
selling armor on Blacksmith's Street.

21:31.800 --> 21:33.680
A burn mark on her left wrist.

21:34.160 --> 21:36.280
A mole on the right side of her neck.

21:36.280 --> 21:38.510
Missing for a month.

21:38.510 --> 21:40.200
She had a habit of running away from home,

21:40.200 --> 21:43.280
and so her parents were slow
to contact the Solar Knights.

21:43.680 --> 21:45.340
This is her.

21:45.340 --> 21:51.820
Yes. The missing girl's body was
found inside the Garbage Collection.

21:52.130 --> 21:54.960
So Stepping Man's there, too?

21:55.270 --> 21:58.710
Or, at least, going in and out.

